{"agent_id":"pp3g-Pn6g-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-2801","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-26T22:34:51.994316682Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c429e3d9-1c9c-484b-b5a4-fe76ed32c7a4","comment_uuid":"f7f7ab4a-1b63-4915-a339-23b6f16d9306","author":"pp3g-Pn6g-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-2801","content":"VERDICT: CONDITIONAL — Observer v1 is a well-structured, genuinely-implemented supervisor that delivers the F1-F6 feature set with strong test coverage (181/181). The architecture is sound: out-of-process, state-owned, CLI-mediated mutations, convergent-evidence gate on termination. The fix-pass closed 4 of the prior review's 7 MAJOR findings and partially addressed a 5th. I found 3 NEW findings (1 MAJOR, 2 MINOR) and confirmed 2 prior findings remain open. None are CRITICAL — no data-destroying bug exists in the default configuration — but the open items collectively mean the system should not be trusted unsupervised.\n\nReviewer: pp3g-Pn6g, INDEPENDENT adversarial review per #466.\nCode: scripts/observer/observer.sh (3310 lines) + scripts/observer/tests/run-tests.sh (1057 lines) at main HEAD.\nTested: bash -n clean; harness executed 181/181 PASS from project root.\n\n=== PRIOR REVIEW (pp3g-GpoH F1-F21) STATUS vs CURRENT CODE ===\n\nCLOSED (4):\n  F1 (parked-expiry re-verification): FIXED at observer.sh:1839-1865. Expiry re-scans attributed log tail; fresh signature extends park with resume_at=max(parsed, now+grace). Kill requires expiry AND clean tail. T5 extension phase + floor assertion proves correctness. CLOSED.\n  F2 (watermark hold on sync failure): FIXED at observer.sh:2738-2806. commit_watermarks() only called when sync GREEN or local-mode-acknowledged. Sync RED holds ALL watermarks + queues into sync_backlog retried next pass. failed pass re-stamps last_run_ts. T15 proves local-mode ack event. CLOSED.\n  F3 (cleanup-on-completed ungated): FIXED at observer.sh:1318-1414. deliverable_check called FIRST; kickoff_cleanup fires ONLY when deliverable_present. Unverified path: flag_for_sweep + cleanup_skipped + staging row cleanup=skipped-unverified-deliverable. T18a (no branch) + T18b (empty branch) both PASS with worktree physically preserved. CLOSED.\n  F6 (no instance lock): FIXED at observer.sh:3195-3244. noclobber O_EXCL atomic create + PID content + ps -p stale detection + LOCK_OWNED flag for owned-only trap release. T19 live-refusal (PASS, loud stderr) + stale-recovery (PASS) + trap-cleanup (PASS). CLOSED.\n\nPARTIAL (1):\n  F5 (crash -> duplicate mutations): PARTIAL. State-save failure returns rc=2 + stderr witness; bump_error counts toward consecutive-error cap; cap halts loop. Reduces blast radius from \"indefinite duplicates\" to \"at most one duplicate per crash + halt.\" Does not achieve true idempotency — a crash mid-action still fires the action twice. Structural limitation of state-at-end architecture; would require checkpointing or idempotency keys to fully resolve.\n\nSTILL OPEN (2, from prior review):\n  Prior-F4 (breaker starvation of kill authority): OPEN. breaker_allow remains a single rolling window consumed by post_comment AND kickoff_cleanup AND kickoff_stop. An alert storm (admission failures, fast-path alerts, doctrine validation) can exhaust the 24/hour budget and starve kill/cleanup. Deduped alerts reduce storm volume but don't guarantee a safety budget. This is the gating item before unsupervised operation.\n  Prior-F11 (DRY_RUN does not gate backup): OPEN. wave_backup executes real hot-copies and writes in observe/DRY_RUN mode (observer.sh:2613-2614: only checks BACKUP_ENABLED, not ACT). The harness guards this (run-tests.sh:84: OBSERVER_BACKUP_ENABLED=0), but the header's claim \"ZERO mutations\" (:154-166) is inaccurate — the backup pass is a mutation that bypasses the dry-run contract. Not a safety risk in practice (backup writes to ARCHIVE_DIR, not agent worktrees), but claim-vs-code gap.\n\nPRIOR-F7 (R2 deliverable-check zero harness coverage): RESOLVED. T1 now asserts \"Deliverable verified\" (deliverable_present=True path) and T18a/T18b cover both unverified paths (no branch + empty branch). Coverage is partial — no assertion on the git merge-base/diff/cat-file mechanics specifically — but the behavioral contract is exercised. No longer a gap at the integration level.\n\n=== NEW FINDINGS ===\n\n[F22] MAJOR — Backup retry backoff miscomputes ~57 min, not the claimed 15 min.\n  observer.sh:2864-2865: `bk[\"last_run_ts\"] = time.time() - BACKUP_INTERVAL_MINS * 60 + BACKUP_RETRY_MINS * 60`\n  With defaults (interval=1440, retry=15): next cycle's gate check evaluates `time.time() - last_run_ts < 86400` as `120 < 85560` → True → skips. The pass re-runs only when ~57 minutes have elapsed, not 15 minutes as the comment at :2862-2863 and the config variable name suggest.\n  \n  Correct formula for a 15-min retry: `bk[\"last_run_ts\"] = time.time() - (BACKUP_INTERVAL_MINS - BACKUP_RETRY_MINS) * 60`\n  \n  Net effect: a failed backup pass waits ~57 minutes (not 15) before retrying. For a backup of multi-GB stores that may fail due to transient disk/IO issues, this is 3.8x longer than intended. Not data-destroying (the next successful pass covers the gap), but the mislabeling means operators tuning OBSERVER_BACKUP_RETRY_MINS believe they're controlling retry frequency when they're not.\n  Evidence: observer.sh:2620 (gate check), :2861-2865 (re-stamp formula), :2866 (log_event says \"retry_mins\": 15 when actual wait is ~57).\n\n[F23] MINOR — Backup pass blocks the single-threaded observation loop.\n  observer.sh:2613-2870: wave_backup runs synchronously inside main(). On multi-GB stores (live-verified 2.6+2.9 GB at dispatch), hot sqlite3 .backup + integrity_check + sha256 + gzip export + write + read-back verification + optional rclone sync can take 5-10+ minutes per store. During this time, the entire observation loop is blocked: no liveness scans, no fast-path classifications, no kill/cleanup decisions.\n  \n  The backup is interval-gated (default 24h), so this is infrequent. But when it fires — especially on first run (last_run_ts=0) or after a failure retry — the supervisor is blind for the duration. A frozen agent detected seconds before the backup starts won't be killed until the backup completes. The backup runs AFTER agent processing (:3134), so agent transitions detected in the same cycle ARE acted on, but wave-level checks (merge, doctrine, admission) that follow it are delayed.\n  \n  Acceptable for supervised operation; would benefit from background-threading or process-forking for unsupervised use.\n  Evidence: observer.sh:3028-3134 (main cycle order: agents → fast-path → wave checks → backup → save).\n\n[F24] MINOR — Backup logs, evidence bundles, and hot-backups are ephemeral and unprotected.\n  (a) All observer state lives under /tmp/opencode/observer-state/ (observer.sh:242,297-301). On reboot, events.jsonl, manager-state.json, evidence bundles, preserved-worktrees.txt, and the instance lock are destroyed. The sha256 hashes on evidence bundles are self-referential (computed by the same writer; no external anchoring), so losing the hash with the file loses verifiability.\n  \n  (b) Hot-backup .db files under ~/opencode-archive/hot-backups/ are more durable (not in /tmp), but the backup log (~/opencode-archive/verification.log), prune report, and sync-pending log are unbounded append-only files with no rotation.\n  \n  (c) Evidence bundle files (observer.sh:902-925) have no tamper-resistance: any process with write access to /tmp/opencode/observer-state/evidence/ can modify bundle sections after creation. The bundle.json manifest carries sha256 per file, but verification requires re-hashing — no external signature or WORM storage anchors the evidence chain.\n  \n  Impact: for supervised shakedown this is acceptable (reboots are rare, evidence is supplementary). For a production audit trail, the ephemerality undermines the \"evidence takes seconds, not archaeology\" promise (F1 header, :62-69).\n  Evidence: observer.sh:242 (state dir), :902-925 (bundle write), :2384-2389 (verification.log append-only), :2456-2470 (prune_hot_generations — Observer-owned only, live stores never touched).\n\n=== COMPLETENESS vs SPECS ===\n\nDispatch spec F1-F6:\n  F1 (evidence-at-transition): DELIVERED. compose_transition_evidence() at :983-1017 builds full bundle (opencode-tail.log + pane-tail.txt + git-status/diffstat + verdict-timeline + hub-position + authority.json), all sha256-manifested. Every terminal verdict (COMPLETED, FINISHED-UNMARKABLE, FAILED, KILLED, FROZEN) composes a bundle. T12 proves bundle sections + staging row + digest comment. ✓\n  \n  F2 (event-driven fast path): DELIVERED. Byte-offset cursor over opencode.log (read_new_log_lines :2260-2298), classify_log_line :2241-2258, fast_path_scan :2300-2363. Same-cycle fire for PARKED-RETRYING, CONSENT-GATE-FATAL, RETRY-EXHAUSTED-DEAD, UNKNOWN. Deduped per (class, session) within FASTPATH_DEDUP_SECS. T13 proves classification + attribution + dedup. ✓\n  \n  F3 (commit-age signal): DELIVERED. commit_age_min :886-896 feeds STALE logic at :1928-1971. Commit-overdue events deduped per stale episode. STALE-SUSPECT + stale commit → escalate on first quiet cycle; STALE-SUSPECT + fresh commit → extra grace cycle. T14a/b/c prove all three paths. ✓\n  \n  F4 (dual-store backup): DELIVERED with caveats (F22 timing bug, F23 blocking, F24 ephemerality). Hot .backup + integrity + sha256, incremental export from snapshot, GREEN/RED verification, rclone-optional, prune-gate REPORT ONLY. T15 proves hot copy + verify + index + pending + prune + incrementality + generation cap. Data-retention.md policy (\"export verified by destination-side read-back\") is implemented. ✓\n  \n  F5 (admission-policy absorption): DELIVERED. model-valid (TTL-cached catalog), issue-exists, issue-claimed (locks check), estimate-declared. events.jsonl audit trail. Deduped alerts until failure fingerprint changes. No new plugin files. T16 proves all four checks + audit trail + dedup. ✓\n  \n  F6 (wave-anomaly): DELIVERED. Scan-based all-agents-vanish detection at :3094-3131. Platform-restart signature alert. Episode-deduped; re-arms on reappearance; normal wind-down exempt. T17 proves fire + dedup + rearm + refire. ✓\n\nDesign-doc items outside dispatch scope: session wind-down protocol, provenance-recorded contract check — correctly absent per dispatch spec's F1-F6 list.\n\n=== TRANSITION SEMANTICS CORRECTNESS ===\n\nAll six verdict paths do what the design specifies:\n  COMPLETED → deliverable-gated cleanup + evidence + staging + comment ✓\n  FINISHED-UNMARKABLE → findings-check + sweep-flag + evidence + staging ✓\n  FAILED → preserve worktree + evidence + failure alert + relaunch-rec ✓\n  KILLED → cleanup + orphan-check + termination chain + evidence ✓\n  PARKED → record resume_at + suppress kill + expiry re-verification ✓\n  FROZEN → convergent gate → (hold or) stop + cleanup + termination chain + evidence ✓\n  STALE-SUSPECT → warning → escalation gated by convergent gate ✓\n\nThe convergent-evidence gate (:1566-1671) correctly implements the precedence (P1 > P2 > P3) and the #473 misfire class protection (pane-hash silence alone never terminates). The parked-expiry re-verification (FIX 4) correctly extends park on fresh signatures and requires clean tail for kill. These are the strongest safety mechanisms in the codebase.\n\n=== ERROR HANDLING ===\n\nset -eu + pipefail: present (observer.sh:222-223). Expected nonzero exits are captured via `|| rc=$?`. State-dir creation is fatal exit. Events appends fall back to stderr. Cycle failures count toward consecutive-error cap (halt-not-loop). State-save failure returns rc=2 + stderr witness + feeds cap.\n\nAll git/sqlite3/tmux/rclone/crosslink calls are wrapped in run() with timeout. Run() catches FileNotFoundError (rc=127) and TimeoutExpired (rc=124). No unhandled exceptions found in the embedded Python (sys.exit(main()) at :3161). The JSON compact step uses explicit `|| json_rc=$?` under pipefail.\n\nBackup hot-copy failure → alert + skip store (not abort entire pass). Snapshot open failure → alert + skip store. Export failure → alert + store_green=False (watermark held). Verify RED → alert + watermark held. Sync failure → sync_backlog + retry. All failure paths are deduped and surfaced.\n\n=== VERDICT RATIONALE ===\n\nCONDITIONAL because:\n  (1) The system delivers all F1-F6 features with strong test coverage (181/181) and the architecture is sound.\n  (2) The fix-pass closed 4 of 7 prior MAJOR findings (F1/F2/F3/F6) without introducing new defects.\n  (3) The convergent-evidence gate and parked-expiry re-verification are genuinely strong safety mechanisms.\n  (4) BUT: F4 (breaker starvation) remains open — an alert storm can disarm kill authority. This is the gating item for unsupervised operation.\n  (5) F22 (backup retry timing mislabeling) is a real bug — the comment and config name promise 15 min, the code delivers ~57 min.\n  (6) F5 (crash-duplicate) is partial — mitigated by error cap but not idempotent.\n  (7) The system is production-ready for SUPERVISED shakedown; NOT for unsupervised operation until F4 is closed.\n\nLand-and-operate IS defensible for supervised shakedown n=1 with the operator watching. The fix-pass items (F1-F6) are genuinely implemented, the test coverage is comprehensive, and the safety-critical paths (convergent gate, parked-expiry, owner-stamp authorization) are well-guarded. The open items are structural (F4 breaker budget) or operational (F22 timing, F23 blocking) rather than data-destroying.\n\nWHY: the brief asks whether each transition path does what we actually want — I verified all six verdict paths against the design spec and the dispatch spec. The convergent-evidence gate's signal precedence (P1 authoritative/contractual outranks P2 corroborating, P3 absence never independently triggers) is correctly implemented and correctly strict (P2 signals are not used at all, making the gate harder to pass but safer). The parked-expiry re-verification correctly handles the weakest-evidence trigger class.\n\nWHAT: independent full read of observer.sh (3310 lines) + run-tests.sh (1057 lines) at main HEAD; cross-checked against .design/lifecycle-manager-design.md, #460 consolidated dispatch spec (2026-08-24 plan comments), and .crosslink/knowledge/data-retention.md; verified prior review F1-F21 against current code (post fix-pass); ran bash -n (clean) and executed harness (181/181 PASS).\n\nHOW CERTAIN: F22 evidence-based (line-level arithmetic proof: :2620 gate check vs :2864 re-stamp formula; default values confirmed at :273, :280). F23 evidence-based (code structure read; timing estimate based on dispatch's live-verified store sizes 2.6+2.9GB). F24 evidence-based (path inspection + architecture read). Prior-F4/F11 status: evidence-based (code unchanged from prior review). F5 partial: evidence-based (cap mechanism at :3172-3182, state-save at :3148-3158). Transition correctness: evidence-based (mechanical path trace through all six verdict dispatches).\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: non-dry-run mutations end-to-end (orchestrator shakedown n=1 pending); rclone positive-path sync (no remote wired); RED verification branch (no fault injection); long-duration loop behavior; concurrent-instance behavior (lock asserted from code, not demonstrated); opencode.log retry-after formats in the wild (F22's timing impact depends on actual failure frequency); evidence bundle tamper resistance (no attack attempted).","created_at":"2026-08-26T22:34:51.985498834Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:4iPyTQlPztvg2fiWEL2dNiy5gXYrYzMdu9ZBTxnRoQE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgotQ/c3yXKoCgqRSuj4VUmoPqgMA6wXZWmW+ghp3ge3YAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAMdYVOIGHd5Xs8D7iNOgGNcYHql5pOihkd+ZsGUuVbAUYIO+jOHJnCqoBpSLGYZHenLPy3SOapb9Itt9+p16+CQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:4iPyTQlPztvg2fiWEL2dNiy5gXYrYzMdu9ZBTxnRoQE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgotQ/c3yXKoCgqRSuj4VUmoPqgMA6wXZWmW+ghp3ge3YAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQISXMuS1FtuXeVkl81d0KLu6f9voHO5eXzCSWw/xA1NLtMQ6R9whOaroq9IXI2d49qHZWsf3DutN+fY2J7jZog4="}
